      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-7901",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We know that the denominator $5x^4+ 2$ is positive for all values of $x.$ So, we can multiply both sides of the inequality by $5x^4+2$ and solve the resulting inequality as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5{x}^{4}+2} & <\\frac{5-2x}{5{x}^{4}+2} \\\\ (5{x}^{4}+2)\\cdot \\frac{2}{5{x}^{4}+2} & <(5{x}^{4}+2)\\cdot \\frac{5-2x}{5{x}^{4}+2} \\\\ 2 & <5-2x \\\\ 2x & <3 \\\\ x & <\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981762/example-7901.json",
          "file_sha256": "670d420148066481aabce859e97c0d4752e07cb8ce1336afebfd707992c2dd75"
